BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (The landmine every practitioner names is the due-on-sale clause. Tim Talks Real Estate spells out the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (mechanics: almost every regular mortgage carries the clause, a wrap almost always transfers the property) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (while the original loan is still open, and the lender can demand the whole balance, not the monthly payment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (but the whole thing, the day they find out [Dklhw3jMfVo @ 00:03:16]. Brian Gibbons calls it the main) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (problem with wraps and adds the buyer-side trap: the seller collects the buyer's payment and then never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (pays the first mortgage [9rVA292DHlY @ 00:01:49]. Gibbons handles both by putting the property in a land) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (trust and routing the buyer's money to a third-party payee that pays the mortgage first and sends the rest to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (the seller. Scott Horne runs the same defense through a loan servicer: buyer pays servicer, servicer pays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (the underlying lender first, seller gets whatever is left. Horne calls it the industry's fraud preventer, because a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (later default can then only mean the buyer missed, not that the seller pocketed the money [VDXOvtqzbZk @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (00:07:47]. Chris Goff wants an escrow company coordinating the monthly payment for the same reason,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (flagging the risk in just paying the seller and hoping the seller is making the payment [X_UODDIMvFs @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (00:06:51].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (The second failure mode is the buyer simply stopping. PrepAgent's Sam-and-Bill example flips from win-win) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (to 'not so fast': if Bill stops paying, Sam cannot pay the existing mortgage, the bank gets angry and it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (becomes a big issue [uHpaHL4qN84 @ 00:02:45]. Shop Rates calls buyer default the biggest risk point) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (because the seller stays legally responsible for the original mortgage, telling sellers to choose their buyers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (wisely and buyers to make sure the seller is financially stable [Z_X2-JRfBYs @ 00:01:26]. Ron LeGrand) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (puts the credit cost on the table: selling on a wrap means nobody pays off the underlying debt, so a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (personally guaranteed loan stays the seller's responsibility for as long as it takes the buyer to cash them out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (With guaranteed debt in play, LeGrand says to be more selective on who goes in the house, or even sell at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (retail price right now and get that debt out of your life [OuQxeQu2HJA @ 00:05:15]. Brian Gibbons adds the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (closing-table bleed: title transfers and a new mortgage or trust deed gets recorded, attorney fees stack on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (top, and if the seller is getting no money down they may refuse to bring cash, so the investor can wind up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (paying all the costs just to get the deal done [9rVA292DHlY @ 00:04:50].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (Then come the economics checks. Maximilian Dier says the place people get in trouble is overpaying: buy at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm ($300,000 on a house only worth $270,000, wrap it out at $280,000 telling yourself you will make it up over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (time, and if the buyer refinances or pays the loan off in full, you are screwed. Dier's rule is to buy under) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (market value with a low interest rate and build in instant equity [49GchpJCUB0 @ 00:09:19]. Bill Brunchick) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (runs the rent-versus-wrap test on high-end homes: a $2,400 all-inclusive payment that only rents for $2,500) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (is not worth the risk, but pushing taxes and insurance onto a wrap buyer and raising the rate can catch a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (spread of $400 to $600 a month with no landlording responsibility [kM__5b36grI @ 00:14:43]. PrepAgent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (sets the floor: to break even, the seller must charge at least as much interest as the existing loan costs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm (which is why sellers negotiate the highest rate they can so the first mortgage gets paid while the deal still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (earns a profit [-8VDqc249XY @ 00:01:35]. Scott Horne's buyer screen is the debt-to-income check run) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.12 Tm (through a residential mortgage loan originator: a 30 percent DTI is pretty reasonable, but at 70 percent the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.90 Tm (bottom line is the buyer cannot afford the house [VDXOvtqzbZk @ 00:06:09].) Tj ET
