BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.10 Tm (liquidated his rentals to pour another $700K in, and the flipper filed bankruptcy owing about $16M. His) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 256.87 Tm (lawsuit rule from his seller-finance teaching is blunt: "The number one deterrent for lawsuits is making sure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.65 Tm (you're not the one that writes the first check" [w1wq3uZtNx8 @ 01:28:46]. Lease options, a structure he) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.42 Tm (says he is obsessed with, burned him once when heirs contested the contract and it cost $7K to sue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.20 Tm (Shena's Mesa duplex shows the investor-side version of the trap: bought in 2021 with 30% down, one unit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 195.97 Tm (vacant for months, listed by an agent for about four months without a sale, until a Sub2 student offered back) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 180.75 Tm (the 30% plus payments in exchange for 0% interest [8VNf8TfmufA @ 00:13:52]. Pace frames that as the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 165.52 Tm (norm rather than the exception, claiming 50% of investors throw the house back on the market within a year) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 150.30 Tm ([8VNf8TfmufA @ 00:14:52].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.07 Tm (The seller side carries its own set of traps. Pace names the biggest downfall in seller finance as sellers) Tj ET
